                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_derived_algebraic_geometry"} In derived algebraic geometry
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            Traditionally, in the strict sense of the term, the
            %em Chern character
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+characteristic+class"} universal characteristic class
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            or equivalently of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            classes, which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational
            combination of all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+classes"} Chern classes
          %p
            This is a special case of the following more general construction (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2Cand+M-Theory"}> Hopkins-Singer 02, section 4.8
            ):
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} representing
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology+theory"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology theory
            there is a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+spectra"} localization
            map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ch
                    %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi E
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ch_E \;\colon\; E \longrightarrow E \wedge H\mathbb{R}
          %p
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "-Chern" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BunkeGepner13"} Bunke-Gepner 13, around def. 2.1
          %p
            In the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            this reproduces the traditional Chern character. (In which case this is a map from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+level"} chromatic level
            1 to chromatic level 0. More generally one can also consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+chromatic+Chern+characters"} higher chromatic Chern characters
            that take values not in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            but in some cohomology theory of higher
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+level"} chromatic level
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+chromatic+Chern+character"} higher chromatic Chern character
            for more on this.)
          %p
            The Chern character
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ch
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ch_E
            may be used to define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            refinements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            by choosing a
            = succeed "-model" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \wedge H\mathbb{R}
            (
            %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger02"}> Hopkins-Singer 02
            , see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+function+complex"} differential function complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ch
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ch_E
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            class associated to a
            %em chern character differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CH
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CH_E
            via the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CH
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CH_E
            has the interpretation of being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+forms"} curvature forms
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            thought of as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} ∞-connections
          %p
            This may be turned around (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"}> Bunke-Nikolaus-Völkl 13, prop. .3.5
            ): given any refinement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{H}
            %a{:href => "cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+--+structures#deRhamCohomology"} de Rham coefficients
            along a Chern character map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ch
                    %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi Π
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Π
                  %msub
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ch_E = \Pi \theta_{\hat E} \;\colon\; E \simeq \Pi(\hat E) \longrightarrow \Pi \flat_{dR} \hat E
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_E
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#differential+cohomology+diagram#HopkinsSingerCoefficients"} differential cohomology diagram – Hopkins-Singer coefficients
          %p
            But more generally, given for instance a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%28n%29-local+spectrum"} K(n)-localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \longrightarrow L_{K(n)} E
            then any choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesive
            refinement of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{K(n)} E
            (i.e. lift through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
            yields a generalized differential cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
            whose intrinsic Chern-character
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi \theta_{\hat E}
            is the
            = succeed "-localization." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(n)
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "differential+cohomology+diagram#ChernCharacterAndFractureSquares"} differential cohomology diagram – Chern character and differential fracture
          %p
            In words this is summarized succintly as:
            %em
              The Chern character is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            Chern characters appear at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson+regulators"} Beilinson regulators
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chow+groups"} Chow groups
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative geometry
            (Chern-Connes character) where the role of usual cohomology is taken by some variant of cyclic cohomology.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#KTheory For vector bundles and topological K-theory
          %p
            The classical theory of the Chern character applies to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            of complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mi KU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = KU
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            operator for some choice of a connection. Consider the symmetric functions in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            variables
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_1,\ldots, t_n
            and let the Chern classes of a complex vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
            (representing a complex K-theory class) be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1,\ldots, c_n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi t
                    %mn 1
                    %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msubsup
                    %mi t
                    %mi n
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi = \phi^n(t_1,\ldots, t_n) = e^{t_1}+\ldots+e^{t_n}= \sum_{k=0}^\infty \frac{1}{k!} (t_1^k+\ldots+t_n^k)
          %p
            Then
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ch(\chi) = \phi(c_1,\ldots,c_n)
          %p
            Let us describe this a bit differently. The cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi KU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^0(X,KU)
            may be represented by a complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deRham+theorem"} deRham theorem
            isomorphism of deRham cohomology with real cohomology) by the even graded closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi j
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ch(\nabla) \coloneqq \sum_{j \in \mathbb{N}}
                  k_j
                  tr( F_\nabla \wedge \cdots \wedge F_\nabla)
                  \\;\;
                  \\in \Omega^{2 \bullet}(X)
                  \\,,
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∇
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
                is any chosen
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
                on the vector bundle;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mo ∇
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi End
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = F_\nabla \in \Omega^2(X,End(V))
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
                of this connection;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_j \in \mathbb{R}
                are normalization constants,
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo !
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi π
                                %mi i
                            %mo )
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_j = \frac{1}{j!} \left( \frac{1}{2\pi i}\right)^j
            %li
              %p
                the trace of the wedge products produces the
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+characteristic+form"} curvature characteristic form
          %p
            The Chern character applied to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney+sum"} Whitney sum
            of two vector bundles is a sum of the Chern characters for the two:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi ch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ch(\xi\oplus \eta) = ch(\chi)+ch(\eta)
            and it is multiplicative under the tensor product of vector bundles:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ch(\xi\otimes\eta)=ch(\chi)ch(\eta)
          %h3#ForSpectraAndGeneralizedCohomology For spectra and generalized cohomology theories
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            it
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represents
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo •
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E^\bullet(X) \;\simeq\; \pi_{-\bullet} Maps(X,E)
          %p
            the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Dold+character"} Chern-Dold character
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            (
            %a{:href => "#Buchstaber70"}> Buchstaber 70
            ) is the map induced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi ℝ
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E \overset{L_{\mathbb{R}}}{\longrightarrow} E_{\mathbb{R}}
          %p i.e. is
          #eq:ChernDoldCharacter.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi chd
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo •
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo •
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo •
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mi 𝔼
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  chd
                  \\;\colon\;
                  E^\bullet(X)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\pi_{-\bullet}Maps(X,E)
                  \\overset{
                  \\pi_{-\bullet}Maps(X,L_{\mathbb{R}})
                  }{\longrightarrow}
                  \\pi_{-\bullet}Maps(X,E_{\mathbb{R}})
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  E^\bullet_{\mathbb{E}}(X)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  H^\bullet(X, \pi_{\bullet}(E)\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}}\mathbb{R})
                  \\,.
          %p
            The very last equivalence in
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ChernDoldCharacter"} (1)
            is due to
            %a{:href => "#Dold56"} Dold 56, Cor. 4
            (reviewed in detail in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Rudyak98"} Rudyak 98, II.3.17
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gross19"} Gross 19, Def. 2.5
          %p
            One place where this neat state of affairs
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ChernDoldCharacter"} (1)
            is made fully explicit is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#LindSatiWesterland16"} Lind-Sati-Westerland 16, Def. 2.1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Buchstaber70"} Buchstaber 70
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Upmeier14"} Upmeier 14
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger02"} Hopkins-Singer 02, Sec. 4.8
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Bunke12"} Bunke 12, Def. 4.45
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BunkeGepner13"} Bunke-Gepner 13, Def. 2.1
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolaus14"} Bunke-Nikolaus 14, p. 17
          %p
            Beware that some authors say
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Dold+character"} Chern-Dold character
            for the full map in
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ChernDoldCharacter"} (1)
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Buchstaber70"} Buchstaber 70
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Upmeier14"} Upmeier 14
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#LindSatiWesterland16"} Lind-Sati-Westerland 16, Def. 2.1
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ChernDoldCharacter"} (1)
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Rudyak98"} Rudyak 98, II.3.17
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gross19"} Gross 19, Def. 2.5
          %p
            Examples of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Dold+characters"} Chern-Dold characters
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
                on
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+character"} Pontrjagin character
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
          %h3#for_cohesive_stable_homotopy_types For cohesive stable homotopy types
          %p
            More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \coloneqq \Pi(\hat E)
            and the corresponding Chern character is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ch
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi Π
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Π
                  %msub
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
