                  ch \coloneqq \Pi \theta_{\hat E} \;\colon\; E \simeq \Pi(\hat E) \longrightarrow \Pi \flat_{dR} \hat E
                  \\,.
          %p
            For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagram"} differential cohomology diagram
          %h3#in_terms_of_cyclic_homology In terms of cyclic homology
          %p
            Generalizing in another direction, generalized Chern characters are given by passage to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+loop+spaces"} derived loop spaces
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+homology"} cyclic homology
            or, more generally,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+cyclic+homology"} topological cyclic homology
            (
            %a{:href => "#ToenVezzosi08"}> Toen-Vezzosi 08
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#HoyoisScherotzkeSibilla15"} Hoyois-Scherotzke-Sibilla 15
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#intertwining_thom_classes_with_todd_classes Intertwining Thom classes with Todd classes
          #RationalToddClassIsChernCharacterOfThomClass.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+Todd+class+is+Chern+character+of+Thom+class"}> rational Todd class is Chern character of Thom class
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundle"} complex vector bundle
              over a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+class"} Todd class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Td
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi ev
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ;
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Td(V) \,\in\, H^{ev}(X; \mathbb{Q})
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+cohomology"} rational cohomology
              equals the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ch
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ch
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+class"} Thom class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} th(V) \,\in\, K\big( Th(V) \big)
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+topological+K-theory"} complex topological K-theory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Th
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th(V)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphisms"} Thom isomorphisms
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi E
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi Th
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_E \;\colon\; E(X) \overset{\simeq}{\to} E\big( Th(V)\big)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Td
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ch
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi_{H\mathbb{Q}}
                    \\big(
                    Td(V)
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    ch\big( th(V) \big)
                    \\,.
            %p
              More generally , for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in K(X)
              any class, we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi Td
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ch
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi_{H\mathbb{Q}}
                    \\big(
                    ch(x)
                    \\cup
                    Td(V)
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    ch\big( \phi_{K}(x) \big)
                    \\,,
            %p
              which specializes to the previous statement for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = 1
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "rational+Todd+class+is+Chern+character+of+Thom+class#Karoubi78"}> Karoubi 78, Chapter V, Theorem 4.4
            )
          %h3#pushforward_and_grothendieckriemannroch_theorem Push-forward and Grothendieck-Riemann-Roch theorem
          %p
            The behaviour of the Chern-character under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+generalized+cohomology"} fiber integration in generalized cohomology
            along
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps"} proper maps
            is described by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck-Riemann-Roch+theorem"} Grothendieck-Riemann-Roch theorem
          %h3#CompatibilityWithTheAdamsOperations Compatibility with the Adams operations
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+operations"} Adams operations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^k
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+topological+K-theory"} complex topological K-theory
            are compatible with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character+map"} Chern character map
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+cohomology"} rational cohomology
            in that the effect of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^k
            on the Chern character image in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2r
            is multiplication by
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^r
          #AdamsLikeOperationsOnRationalCohomology.num_defn
