                )
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Chern+character"} equivariant Chern character
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
          %ul
            %li#Stefanich
              German Stefanich,
              %em Chern Character in Twisted and Equivariant K-Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://math.berkeley.edu/~germans/Chern2.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h3#cherndold_character_on_generalized_cohomology Chern-Dold character on generalized cohomology
          %p
            The identification of rational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized cohomology
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the rationalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Dold56
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albrecht+Dold"}> Albrecht Dold
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Relations between ordinary and extraordinary homology
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "http://mi.mathnet.ru/eng/mat350"} mathnet:mat350
              %em Algebraic Topology: A Student’s Guide
              (London Mathematical Society Lecture Note Series, pp. 166-177). Cambridge: Cambridge University Press 1972 (
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511662584.015"}> doi:10.1017/CBO9780511662584.015
              )
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Hilton71"} Hilton 71, Theorem 3.18
            %li#Rudyak98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuli+Rudyak"}> Yuli Rudyak
                , II.7.13 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Thom Spectra, Orientability, and Cobordism
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9
            %li#Gross19
              %p
                Jacob Gross,
                %em The homology of moduli stacks of complexes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.03269"}> arXiv:1907.03269
                )
          %p
            The combination of
            %a{:href => "#Dold56"} Dold 56
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Dold+character"} Chern-Dold character
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology+theory"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology theory
            is due (for
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology"} complex cobordism cohomology
          %ul
            %li#Buchstaber70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Buchstaber"}> Victor Buchstaber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Chern–Dold character in cobordisms. I
              %p
                Russian original: Mat. Sb. (N.S.), 1970 Volume 83(125), Number 4(12), Pages 575–595 (
                %a{:href => "http://m.mathnet.ru/php/archive.phtml?wshow=paper&jrnid=sm&paperid=3530&option_lang=eng"}> mathnet:3530
                )
              %p
                English translation: Mathematics of the USSR-Sbornik, Volume 12, Number 4, AMS 1970 (
                %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1070/SM1970v012n04ABEH000939"}> doi:10.1070/SM1970v012n04ABEH000939
                )
          %p Review in
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#Hilton71"} Hilton 71, p. 50
          %p That the Chern-Dold character reduces to the original Chern character on K-theory is
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#Hilton71"}> Hilton 71, Theorem 5.8
              \.
          %p That the Chern-Dold character is given by rationalization of representing spectra is made fully explicit in
          %ul
            %li#LindSatiWesterland16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Lind"}> John Lind
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Craig+Westerland"} Craig Westerland
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twisted iterated algebraic K-theory and topological T-duality for sphere bundles
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.06285"} arXiv:1601.06285
          %p
            This rationalization construction appears also (without attribution to
            %a{:href => "#Hilton71"} #Hilton 71
            or
            %a{:href => "#Buchstaber70"} Buchstaber 70
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Dold56"} Dold 56
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsSinger02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0211/0211216v2.pdf#page=47"} 4.8, page 47
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2Cand+M-Theory"} Quadratic Functions in Geometry, Topology,and M-Theory
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0211216"} math.AT/0211216
            %li#Bunke12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                %em Differential cohomology
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1208.3961"}> arXiv:1208.3961
                )
            %li#BunkeGepner13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
                %em Differential function spectra, the differential Becker-Gottlieb transfer, and applications to differential algebraic K-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.0247"}> arXiv:1306.0247
                )
            %li#Upmeier14
              %p
                Markus Upmeier,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Refinements of the Chern-Dold Character: Cocycle Additions in Differential Cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.2027"} arXiv:1404.2027
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40062-015-0106-y"} doi:10.1007/s40062-015-0106-y
            %li#BunkeNikolaus14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twisted differential cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1406.3231"} arXiv:1406.3231
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.agt/1566439272"} euclid:euclid.agt/1566439272
          %p
            More on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Dold+character"} Chern-Dold character
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology"} complex cobordism cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Buchstaber"}> Victor Buchstaber
              , A. P. Veselov,
              %em Chern-Dold character in complex cobordisms and abelian varieties
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.05782"}> arXiv:2007.05782
              )
          %p
            The observation putting this into the general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagrams"} differential cohomology diagrams
            (see there) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"} stable homotopy types
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V%C3%B6lkl"} Michael Völkl
              %em Differential cohomology theories as sheaves of spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3188"}> arXiv:1311.3188
              )
          %p
            based on
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BunkeGepner13"} Bunke-Gepner 13
          %p
            Further generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Dold+character"} Chern-Dold character
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian cohomology
          %ul
            %li#FSS20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+Character+Map+in+Twisted+Non-Abelian+Cohomology"} The Character Map in Nonabelian Cohomology — Twisted, Differential, Generalizaed
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.11909"} arXiv:2009.11909
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/13422"} doi:10.1142/13422
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Chern-Dold+character"} equivariant Chern-Dold character
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
          %ul
            %li
